# Target B — jammed shell-stability route

Target B is the first-order-jammed branch. The shared theory forces an almost-rhombic
contact complex, after which the remaining issue is a quantitative boundary/shell
stability statement.

## Route module

- [01 — Jammed almost-rhombic branch](01-jammed-rhombic-branch.md): perimeter and
  width saturation, train-angle identities, phase energy, backward-train mechanisms,
  fixed-angle and affine-lattice exclusion, and the exact Target B frontier
  (Sections 24–56).

## Promoted audited addenda

- [Phase cuts and coherent crossing families](../../reports/target_b_phase_cut_and_biclique_2026-09-05.md)
  proves **PC**, **PW**, **CR**, **PS**, **IS**, **TS**, and **NE**, records the
  **SI** interval-biclique regression, and corrects the
  Section 52 equality wording
  (**EC**). PC deletes at most `floor(3 Delta / pi)` crossing relations, hence
  only `O(D)`, to obtain an exact real acyclic phase potential on the full train
  graph. The dense components of Section 50 are themselves acyclic for large `D`.
  CR proves `D >= (a+b) cos(pi/6+2 epsilon)-2` for a complete coherent crossing
  family in a pure disk, without an additive-block hypothesis. PS consequently
  excludes the core-sized coherent phase-star endpoint, even when its smaller
  class has vanishing relative size. IS extracts a large complete crossing family
  from a nearly complete coherent pair using its ordered intervals. TS proves
  balanced tripartite stability. Together they give NE: a uniform exclusion of
  coherent, core-sized, near-extremal three-class train graphs. These statements
  supersede the corresponding feedback-set, long-cycle, additive-realization, and
  coherent near-equality gaps in Sections 49–56. PC4 gives a global phase-class
  reduction after only `O(D)` omitted crossings: PW forces a linear-size phase
  window whenever retained crossing density is quadratic. A survivor is then
  phase-imbalanced at quadratic scale or has a quadratic deficit from every phase
  split. NE eliminates the former when its coherent core hypotheses hold; the
  latter is the remaining phase-density obstruction. The addendum also proves
  **HA**, the edge-aligned-hole estimate
  `G_holes >= (sqrt(3)/4) B_holes - (sqrt(3)/2) h`, matching the Euler
  correction for `h` holes.

- [Independent dense-grid / penetration / interpolation audit](../../reports/target_b_dense_grid_penetration_interpolation_dependency_audit_2026-09-11.md)
  promotes the corrected downstream tools under their exact scopes. **DT1–DT4**
  replace the false global linear-stack claim by the complement-dual tree and its
  almost-spanning backbone extraction. **TG1–TG3** give deep-grid penetration and
  exclude complete coherent phase stars carrying the quadratic core. **PDG** turns
  crossing density `rho` into a complete rectangle with shores at least
  `rho^2 M/128` and `rho b/4-O(1)`. **PC1/PC3** charge arbitrary diagonal
  cancellation by physical grid crossings and deleted-interface crossings.
  **MCP1/MCP2** aggregate these charges with multiplicity at most two; the additive
  MCP2 form is read with fixed Section-50 `lambda`, which gives only
  `O_lambda(1)` retained components and hence a summed `o(D^2)` coherence error.
  Finally **GPI** proves, for one dominant coherent component with
  `M>=b>=a`, `t=b/M>=tau>0`, and local Theorem-51 deficit `Delta`,
  `liminf Delta >= 4e-17 tau^2`. This is a local dominant-component theorem, not a
  multi-grain globalization.

## Audited-working advance: exact boundary backtracking

- [Section 120 boundary-backtracking hostile audit](120-boundary-backtracking-audit.md)
  certifies the old proposed equation (37.7) in the simply connected pure
  strict-rhombic disk. For either outer-boundary arc `Gamma` joining an active
  diameter pair, train crosscut orientation supplies one injectively charged
  terminal edge for every separating train. If `P_0` and `P_-` are the tangent and
  backward separating trains and `S_-` is the total backward signed weight, then
  `|Gamma|-D >= |P_0|+|P_-|+S_-/D`. Hence
  `S_- <= D(|Gamma|-D)/2` and `|P_0|+|P_-| <= |Gamma|-D`. The same theorem bounds
  all positive quadratic curvature of one active diameter bar by its boundary
  detour. It does **not** prove a universal quartic-blocker rank bound or the
  component-quotiented blocker/coforest inequality, so Target B remains open.

## Exact remaining endpoint

A sufficient closure is the joint outer-shell stability inequality
`Oler surplus >= (sqrt(3)/4) P`, equivalently
`G+E >= (sqrt(3)/4) B + (sqrt(3)/2)(t+chi-1)` with the canonical topology
corrections. The strict global-minimizer allowance is the reverse inequality
(Section 36). The current record does not prove this closure.

The phase-star and coherent near-extremal core subcases are excluded by PS/NE, and
the dense-grid/penetration/GPI tools are now independently certified. The live
pure-disk obstruction is global rather than local class-size interpolation:
several linearly sized coherent grains may share the quadratic crossing mass, while
PDG's density-only grid can remain below the `2D/sqrt(3)` PC3 cancellation threshold.
A closure must couple retained physical crossings, deleted/interface crossings, and
virtual noncrossing determinant mass across all macroscopic grains, or turn the
phase potential into an actual strict smaller-diameter competitor while controlling
active diameter constraints. No such global inequality or competitor theorem is
proved. The general topology correction and flexible branch remain necessary.
Target B stays separate from Target A because plain shell/area bookkeeping does not
control source-capacity deficit.

